<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Turkey: 162 arrested in LGBTQ+ raids</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05b63fb4a70ff10269aa66b84864fb99949f95c2a848ddd8991e922bc983bdff</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:32Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-162-arrested-in-lgbtq-raids/a-79251409--cfa34afe3cef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-162-arrested-in-lgbtq-raids/a-79251409?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Turkish authorities have arrested at least 162 people in a weekend crackdown on the country's LGBTQ+ community. Ankara says police raids on gay bars and other venues are aimed at protecting family values.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, Poland say Russia hit Warsaw-bound passenger train</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d783aecbeceb6b292697dfaaac71e751baced96cf64e27149dfab958b000e1c8</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T12:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-poland-say-russia-hit-warsaw-bound-passenger-train/a-79251428--fddf046eb6b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-poland-say-russia-hit-warsaw-bound-passenger-train/a-79251428?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian officials accused Russia of a "systemic attack" on its railways following drone strikes near the Polish border, including a hit on a locomotive of a passenger train headed to Warsaw.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russians on the Goethe-Institut: 'Hostage to politics'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aca4be5cfa1727d960132872050f278ce97b5c7878551aecdbe5d33769e2bf04</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:38Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T11:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936--8619b68c7998.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russians-on-the-goethe-institut-hostage-to-politics/a-79218936?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canceled language exams, disrupted plans to study in Germany, and the disappearance of an important cultural link: DW users shared how the closure of Germany's Goethe-Institut in Russia affects their lives.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Croatia: 'Monster' fire triggers evacuation on Brac island</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b02034438a82ba52af38dfa6faa9c295e1ebe9255a9c22eeca9045ab746c4477</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T10:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/croatia-monster-fire-triggers-evacuation-on-brac-island/a-79250480--68433f30b29b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/croatia-monster-fire-triggers-evacuation-on-brac-island/a-79250480?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A rapidly spreading wildfire threatened homes and tourist accommodations on the Croatian island of Brac, with firefighters battling the blaze overnight.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Vanuatu ferry capsize leaves one dead, 30 missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a884b9c6ff2d290bac41a88e495ed1f0eacefc3ba5e5524505055f94a907897c</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T10:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/vanuatu-ferry-capsize-leaves-one-dead-30-missing/a-79249954--620cbead1598.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/vanuatu-ferry-capsize-leaves-one-dead-30-missing/a-79249954?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rescue efforts have been slow after a South Pacific inter-island ferry sank in bad weather on Friday. An investigation has already begun into negligence on the part of the operator.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia rescuers search for 130 people after ferry sinks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1306316244b9f22cdc4cb5a849be6016c207380f8edfbd08a607e93ef5107850</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:46Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-rescuers-search-for-130-people-after-ferry-sinks/a-79248600--c82a5db62e93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-rescuers-search-for-130-people-after-ferry-sinks/a-79248600?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The ship was carrying over 240 people in the Java Sea when it ran into bad weather. Officials say six people have died and 130 are still missing.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Lower Saxony local polls in focus after AfD win</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:03a3951c9040a401bb1507701e0a1d4df5bcab4ab2948c575639b07184545293</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:50Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T08:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-lower-saxony-local-polls-in-focus-after-afd-win/live-79223427--1dd3f476214d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-lower-saxony-local-polls-in-focus-after-afd-win/live-79223427?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The northwestern state of Lower Saxony is holding local elections that are being seen as a gauge of support for the far-right AfD party. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>A Romani artist in Hungary reclaims his identity</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b41a72da46079df122adfe42351e4fe760121a431f604bf9ba6f2917f881f853</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:22:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266--3fed9cef9147.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-romani-artist-in-hungary-reclaims-his-identity/a-79247266?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Norbert Olah is an artist. He's also Romani. For a long time, he avoided making his ethnic background a theme of his art for fear of being pigeonholed. Then it became his focus.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden election: Far right eyes power for 1st time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f292fca2da0dfede822e3b5f9f82c0906399f896dc98b80300a7425efa9fc8b7</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T06:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sweden-election-far-right-eyes-power-for-1st-time/a-79248599--5a0c9f3ecce9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sweden-election-far-right-eyes-power-for-1st-time/a-79248599?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The populist Sweden Democrats could enter government for the first time if incumbent Ulf Kristersson's bloc wins. The left-wing opposition led by former PM Andersson has seen its lead narrow as election day has neared.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Attack ruled out in train derailment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5a1ba1bf4b6033abf99eb48e2455c8ca5d3151c012f6ce6c76b560ef34b9a08e</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T01:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-attack-ruled-out-in-train-derailment/a-79241365--79cb5d1cf8aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-attack-ruled-out-in-train-derailment/a-79241365?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">More than 40 were injured when a train derailed between Rouen and Caen in Normandy, northwest France, on Friday evening. Investigators say there is "no indication" the incident was deliberate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Anthropic boss Dario Amodei calls for AI slowdown</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:486fc537b6860d512b8e5de156a53d98a93a1a1c61e9d52a2178ed286977d2bd</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T23:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/anthropic-boss-dario-amodei-calls-for-ai-slowdown/a-79247690--c49b3d4a8d56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/anthropic-boss-dario-amodei-calls-for-ai-slowdown/a-79247690?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk and OpenAI chief Sam Altman say they agree with Amodei's view that safety measures need time to catch up to AI's rapid development, after a recent hacking incident by AI agents.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Baghdad confirms attack on Saudi pipeline came from Iraq</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5772465d4fbc259c742bb9ce844c4cb54b48beb2640121bb9a474e3e56173bfc</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T20:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/baghdad-confirms-attack-on-saudi-pipeline-came-from-iraq/a-79247086--0adeea375bd8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/baghdad-confirms-attack-on-saudi-pipeline-came-from-iraq/a-79247086?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Saudi Arabia has said it will not retaliate and wants Iraq to "take the necessary measures." Baghdad is under pressure from the United States to rein in Iran-backed militias.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why are European banks moving gold out of United States?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22138a946fb06f290fba64654d28c243b407cc2be507ad3efa9d23928d73ac88</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T15:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-gold-out-of-united-states/a-79213013--320ff1551fa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-are-european-banks-moving-gold-out-of-united-states/a-79213013?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Netherlands and France have moved their gold out of US vaults. Part of the reason is fears about the reliability of the US, but equally important is the need to keep gold closer to home in the event of a crisis.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Several killed in series of Russian strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27edd122fe23e9ca6273f659311c165236e6e42341bc2e6bbc96546f63d21fba</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T15:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-several-killed-in-series-of-russian-strikes/a-79245980--1c9c8b0bb81c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-several-killed-in-series-of-russian-strikes/a-79245980?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Local authorities said several civilians were killed and dozens more wounded across Ukraine by Russian strikes. Meanwhile, the Kremlin has rejected Volodymyr Zelenskyy's proposal to meet with the Russian leader in Miami.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria: Fire at factory making munitions for Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cea039377707fb4e530c70d01ccb86f9fb06f7b2913616a7b0c0be08b1b1578f</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T12:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-fire-at-factory-making-munitions-for-ukraine/a-79245062--ffd8d661930f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-fire-at-factory-making-munitions-for-ukraine/a-79245062?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bulgarian authorities are investigating a fire at a munitions factory for links to an explosion at a similar facility in August. Arms maker EMCO says no human error was involved, as investigators look at sabotage.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump visits Ireland, says unification would be 'fantastic'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:026a8add63a6605b2b27ee73176d6551fb61a1447cedd29ea187603bdcc430c0</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-visits-ireland-says-unification-would-be-fantastic/a-79244685--23dd10281a51.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-visits-ireland-says-unification-would-be-fantastic/a-79244685?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's trip to Ireland to watch a golf tournament has also included meetings with leaders there.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda lays 'boy king' Oyo to rest amid succession row</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a33af0135fc0218754ee43ecf908c5fc5443f823a8a6aea67709467ec52d0a75</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-lays-boy-king-oyo-to-rest-amid-succession-row/a-79243428--755cb45ab2c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-lays-boy-king-oyo-to-rest-amid-succession-row/a-79243428?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Uganda has buried King Oyo Nyimba, who was crowned in the Tooro Kingdom in 1995 aged just 3. His death at 34 has triggered a dispute over a successor, as rumors abound of possible heirs born out of wedlock.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>BRICS summit leaders urge 'maximum restraint' in Middle East</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63fbdd7e4840778d6a66b01901c07ae2db0fa41232469b61cca654063387dd91</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brics-summit-leaders-urge-maximum-restraint-in-middle-east/live-79224239--4541a165cd4b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brics-summit-leaders-urge-maximum-restraint-in-middle-east/live-79224239?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The joint declaration at the BRICS 2026 summit expressed 'deep concern' over hostilities in the Middle East. China's President Xi Jinping said the Iran war was not in the bloc's interest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian GRU spies behind failed Leipzig attack: reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e35bfec078c46ec24669e15247c5853e77fbe4e5bf0e50a4461ef9c6eca18b5d</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-gru-spies-behind-failed-leipzig-attack-reports/a-79244858--97143d694fa7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-gru-spies-behind-failed-leipzig-attack-reports/a-79244858?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A German newspaper has cited reports tying a failed attack at Leipzig Airport to Moscow's GRU military intelligence agency. One suspect's ties to GRU were known when he entered the country, yet he was not surveilled.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Flavio Bolsonaro faces corruption probe weeks before election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb95c75de9a687e00f00743f0ab12cd2ef8fff8ef67b529ea38791901fd1a783</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T09:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-faces-corruption-probe-weeks-before-election/a-79242561--f6206eb40070.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-flavio-bolsonaro-faces-corruption-probe-weeks-before-election/a-79242561?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brazilian Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, Lula's top rival in next month's election, is under investigation for alleged corruption linked to financing a biopic about his father, former President Jair Bolsonaro.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Corals as climate archive: Are El Ninos intensifying?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2a33157da21fc07e58ad5f394e38d9a2b412d3d5c012b8121320acac9792931</id><updated>2026-09-13T13:21:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-12T08:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-ninos-intensifying/a-79243425--052f407fd862.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/corals-as-climate-archive-are-el-ninos-intensifying/a-79243425?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Records from the past few decades show that, during this period, El Nino events have been frequent and often extreme. But is this normal, or is it the result of climate change? Corals can give us a clear indication.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
